<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Panama's Wildlife – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin-top: 10px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 7th Grade (CEFR: A2.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Wildlife</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> The Habitat of Wildlife</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write instructions for a simple game or craft. Interactive: Write simple comments on a peer's short text.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write instructions for a wildlife guessing game (e.g., "Choose an animal card and describe its habitat."). Can provide steps for a nature craft related to animals (e.g., "Cut out shapes to make a sloth."). Can write supportive comments on a peer's description of wildlife (e.g., "I like your information about the jaguar.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 25px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; width: 15%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of various Panamanian wildlife (e.g., jaguar, sloth, harpy eagle, frog, snake) and their habitats (forest, jungle, trees, rivers). Students brainstorm orally in pairs, listing animals and describing where they live. Example: "This is a jaguar. It lives in the forest." The teacher writes key vocabulary on the board (habitat, forest, jungle, live, protect).</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students then write down 2-3 sentences about an animal and its habitat based on the pictures, focusing on simple descriptive sentences.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing simple, clear instructions on the board for a "Guess the Animal" game, emphasizing sequence words (First, Next, Then, Finally). Example: "First, choose an animal. Next, describe its habitat. Then, your partner guesses. Finally, change roles." The teacher also models describing an animal using comparatives: "The jaguar is faster than the sloth."</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher clearly pronounces key vocabulary, highlighting long and short vowel sounds: /sneɪk/ 'snake', /iːg/ 'eagle', /frɒg/ 'frog', /bæt/ 'bat'.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What words do we use to show the order of steps?" (Expected answer: First, Next, Then, Finally.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I write 'The sloth moves slowly', what kind of word is 'slowly'?" (Expected answer: An adverb.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What information should your instructions give?" (Expected answer: How to play the game/make the craft.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents two short texts on a projector or handout:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Text 1: Instructions for a simple "Sloth Nature Craft"</b> (genre: instructional, register: informal, format: bulleted list with illustrations).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "<b>How to Make a Sloth Mask:</b> 1. Cut out a circle for the face. 2. Draw big eyes. 3. Use brown paper for the fur. Sloths live in the forest. They are slow, but they survive."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Text 2: A short paragraph describing a Panamanian animal's habitat and habits.</b></li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "The Harpy Eagle: This incredible predator lives in the dense jungle of Panama. It hunts monkeys and sloths. There are not many harpy eagles; they are an endangered species. It is larger than most other birds."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Written Expression: Production of short, clear instructional texts and descriptive paragraphs using appropriate vocabulary and grammar for A2.2 level.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read Text 1 and identify the verbs used for actions (e.g., "cut out," "draw," "use").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read Text 2 and underline all the adjectives describing the harpy eagle or its habitat (e.g., "incredible," "dense," "endangered," "larger"). They also identify sentences using "There is/are" and present simple verbs.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences describing habitats using "There is/there are," present simple verbs, and comparative/superlative adjectives. They will also practice writing simple, sequential instructions using target vocabulary.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> Students complete sentences with appropriate vocabulary or grammar.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1: "There _____ many different ______ (species/animals) in the Panamanian ______ (forest/jungle)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2: "The hummingbird is _____ (fast) than the sloth." (Students choose correct comparative form).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3: Students reorder jumbled words to form instructions: "animal / an / Choose / First." -> "First, choose an animal."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Instruction Writing):</b> In pairs, students receive a set of verbs (e.g., 'cut', 'glue', 'draw', 'choose', 'describe', 'guess') and habitat vocabulary. They must write 3-4 steps for a simple "Animal Puppet Craft" or "Animal Habitat Guessing Game" using sequence words (First, Next, Then, Finally) and the provided vocabulary. Example: "First, choose a wild animal like a jaguar. Next, draw its habitat. Then, write two facts about how it adapts."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Feedback & Revision:</b> Pairs exchange their written instructions from activity 2 with another pair. They check for correct grammar (present simple, there is/are), appropriate vocabulary (endangered, nocturnal, wild), clarity, and logical sequence. Students write simple comments like, "Good use of 'First'!" or "Check verb form for 'live'." (Pragmatic: Using comparatives: "Your description is clearer than mine.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students) to create a set of written instructions for a "Panama Wildlife Habitat Guessing Game" or a "Panama Wildlife Craft" (e.g., making a miniature habitat diorama or an animal mask). Each group chooses one activity.</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative written product. Each group must produce a clear set of 4-6 step instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Instructions Requirements:</b>
                        <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use at least three sequence words (First, Next, Then, Finally).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least five vocabulary words related to "The Habitat of Wildlife" (e.g., habitat, forest, jungle, protect, endangered, live, adapt, species, biodiversity).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporate at least one sentence using "There is/there are" to describe elements in the habitat.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Include at least one sentence using a comparative or superlative adjective to describe an animal or its feature (e.g., "The sloth is slower than the monkey.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ensure the instructions are logical and easy to follow. (Sociolinguistic: Facilitate group discussions and follow instructions.)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups write their instructions on a large sheet of paper or a digital document.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer assessment using a checklist and teacher observation during group work and final product review.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group posts their written instructions. Students walk around the classroom and read other groups' instructions. They select one set of instructions and write a supportive comment on a sticky note or on the paper, using simple phrases.</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example comments: "I like your idea for the craft!" "Your steps are very clear." "Good use of 'endangered'!" "The jaguar description is great."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher & Peer Check):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and logical sequence of instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of sequence words (First, Next, Then, Finally).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., habitat, wildlife, forest, endangered).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of "There is/there are" and present simple for descriptions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of comparative/superlative adjectives.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Legibility and overall presentation.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer two questions individually:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. What was easy or difficult when writing the instructions today?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Write one new word or grammar rule you used correctly today.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">7-8 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Consolidation and Planning)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. How well did my group work together to write the instructions?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. What is one thing I will remember about writing instructions for a game or craft?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this writing lesson? (e.g., students effectively used sequence words, applied comparative adjectives, engaged in peer feedback).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What challenges did students face during the writing process? (e.g., consistent use of "there is/are," spelling of new vocabulary, sentence structure).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to improve writing fluency and accuracy? (e.g., more sentence structure practice, dedicated vocabulary review, visual aids for grammar points).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will use the written instructions and descriptions from today's lesson as a basis for a 21st Century Skills Project, possibly creating a multimedia presentation or a display about Panama's wildlife and its habitats, summarizing and explaining their chosen animal or craft to a wider audience.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>